      "receiptId": "fat-rascals.html-1",
      "receiptSource": "The original source of this receipt isn\u0027t known. Can you help? \u003Ca href=\u0022mailto:editor@foodsofengland.co.uk?subject=Foods%20of%20England,%20Fat%20Rascals\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003Eeditor@foodsofengland.co.uk\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003EFat Rascals\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\n2 oz lard\u003Cbr\u003E\n2 oz butter\u003Cbr\u003E\n10 oz plain flour\u003Cbr\u003E\n3 oz currants\u003Cbr\u003E\n2 oz candied mixed peel\u003Cbr\u003E\n1 heaped tsp baking powder\u003Cbr\u003E\n3 oz caster sugar\u003Cbr\u003E\n6 oz whipping cream, slightly soured\u003Cbr\u003E\nglace cherries and blanched almond, for decoration\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\nRub the fat into flour, add the dry ingredients and mix with the cream to a stiff paste. Roll out to \u00BE inch thickness and cut into rounds. Decorate the surface with a cherry and two or thre almonds. Brush with milk. Bake at 425 \u00B0F / Gas 7 on a floured sheet for 10-15 minutes.\u003Cbr\u003E"
    }
